From 6b719258c5c4ddfe91c8c299cdf5a5cc2e9172d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 15:41:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] battery: report the pack's design capacity and the driver's
 verdict on it

"Is this battery worn out?" has not been answerable from nyx. The pieces
were nearly all there: battery_full40() reads how much the gauge believes
the pack holds now, and nyx_battery_status_t has had an unused health field
since LG wrote it. What was missing is the number that makes the first one
mean anything - what the pack held when it was new - and anyone to fill in
the second.

Add battery_full_design(), reading charge_full_design, and battery_health(),
mapping the driver's own "health" string onto nyx_battery_health_t.
Deliberately no fallback from design capacity to charge_full: answering the
design question with the present capacity would report every pack in the
world as factory fresh, which is worse than not answering.

The two full-capacity attributes also learn to look at the BMS. How big a
pack is, and how big it used to be, are fuel-gauge questions, and the supply
of type "Battery" is not always the fuel gauge: on Qualcomm platforms the
charger driver owns that supply while a separate one of type "BMS" is the
gauge. A tissot has charge_full on both and charge_full_design only on the
BMS, so asking the battery supply alone says "this pack has no factory
capacity" about a pack that publishes one a directory away. Only these two
fall back - the readings that describe a moment, voltage and current and
temperature and charge, stay on the supply the module picked, so nothing
starts silently mixing two sources for the same instant.

Tests cover both readers: design capacity present, absent, on the BMS only,
on both (the battery supply wins), and on neither; every health string the
kernel defines, mixed case, and an unrecognised one staying UNKNOWN rather
than becoming a guess.

Resolving a battery's paths now asks whether the two full-capacity
attributes exist, and it does that for every battery found, not only the one
a test set up. The g_file_test mock answers "not there" for those two on any
node it does not know rather than every test having to declare paths it does
not use; everything else still asserts on an unexpected path.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>

Upstream-Status: Pending [carried until the fix is merged in the
webOS-ports nyx-modules fork and SRCREV moves]
